      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, positive material parameters yield positive c, and the inherited acoustic equations yield transport of the negative mode. Geometric translation gives both profile identities. Differentiable profiles satisfy the classical transport equation by the one-variable chain rule, and its converse follows from the spatial slice at time zero. Locally integrable profiles satisfy the oriented rectangle identity with flux −cq by affine changes of variables; positivity of c ensures boundary-flux slices are integrable. Conversely, the balance predicate already requires integrability of the time-zero spatial slice f. Thus the two equivalences express the selected domains without an additional uniqueness or completeness claim. The printed passage alone does not fix these conventions."
